extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 82-84 (cache p083-p085, text layer, page_offset +1). The Tech-Ninja O.C.C. heading is mid-column on printed 82 after the Cyber-Samurai''s closing lines; the entry ends with the Money and Cybernetics lines at the top of printed 84, where the Ninja Juicer begins. Printed 82 and 83 were rendered and match the text layer. || GROUP: the contents (printed 4) files the class under Character Classes of the Republic chapter, which names no group. Stored as men-of-arms with men_of_arms true because it is a trained assassin built on Hand to Hand combat, like the Mystic Ninja. A judgment call. || XP: the Tech-Ninja, Mystic Ninja column of the Experience Point Tables (cache p217), read off a render. || SKILLS: Japanese is stored as Language: Native Tongue (catalog 98%; the +20% cannot raise it) and Literacy: Native Language at 40 +15. Disguise (+10%) is printed twice in the O.C.C. skills and is stored once; the duplicate grants nothing. Imitate Voice and Impersonation (+10%) is stored as the catalog''s two skills, Imitate Voices & Sounds (42+10) and Impersonation (30+10), following the Rifts Changeling precedent. Medical''s criminal sciences and forensics is the catalog''s Forensics. Secondary skills: five, from the related list without its bonuses. || HAND TO HAND: Assassin; changing to Ninjitsu costs three other skills (the related picks) and to Aikido, Jujitsu or Karate one. The Ninjitsu condition is shown, not enforced. || EQUIPMENT: the energy weapon, E-clip type, grenades, vibro-blade and ancient weapon are choices over catalog rows because the book names none. The book gives 4D4x1000 credits worth of black market salable items besides the 3D6x1000 credits; the items are not coin and are prose. The 1D4 implants of choice cannot be a dice-count choice and are prose. The micro-film camera and small crowbar are this book''s micro-film-camera and small-crowbar rows (printed 83)."
