## Lore

The ninja clans did not die with the old world. They survived the centuries by growing ever more secretive, and even the chaos after the coming of the Rifts could not wipe them out. The post-apocalyptic age produced two kinds of ninja: the traditional mystic shadow warrior, and a modern counterpart, the tech-ninja (also called cyber-ninja or ninja-techie).

Tech-ninja serve Japan''s corporations, whose rivalries can turn brutal and even deadly. They carry out espionage, sabotage and the occasional assassination or kidnapping against a patron''s business rivals. Every major corporation, Ichto and H-Brand among them, keeps a stable or clan of tech-ninja. H-Brand even hires its clan out to other nations, gaining a larger force and a steady trickle of secrets, and has enhanced a third of its ninja with full bionic conversion and juicer and crazy augmentation.

Unlike the traditional clans, which trace their families back for centuries, tech-ninja are recruited: mostly orphans and unwanted children, adopted or taken very young, raised to be loyal to the clan and to trust no outsider. Deceit is encouraged from childhood, and secrecy is kept at all costs.

Tech-ninja specialize in espionage, silent and covert operations and other illicit work. Most live seemingly normal lives, masquerading as businessmen, police officers (some joined the force already in the clan''s service) or soldiers, and some join mercenary or adventurer groups, never forgetting that their first loyalty is to the clan. They are trained in stealth, hand to hand combat and evasion, mostly for the city rather than the wilderness, with emphasis on defeating security systems and computer hacking. The wet work is usually left to specialists: the ninja ''borgs, juicers and crazies. The typical tech-ninja is expected to pass as an executive, break into a corporate president''s office, hack his computer and leave by the top floor of the skyscraper.

The traditional clans hold the tech-ninja in contempt as imitators who sully the ninja name; the tech-ninja think the traditionalists are dinosaurs, and claim their cybernetics, juicers and ''borgs outmatch any mystic art. In the New Republic a few corporations keep small teams and keep their activities low, and some benevolent corporations have lent their ninja to the government for covert operations, including raids on H-Brand and on the oni regions. In return the government overlooks occasional industrial espionage, as long as no innocents are harmed.

## Player Notes

Working among non-ninja, a tech-ninja player character usually poses as a high-tech thief or city rat, a spy, or a warrior or adventurer. If the other characters serve the same corporation as his clan, he might reveal his true profession, but only once he is convinced he can trust them.

## Equipment and Money

Beyond the listed gear, the equipment section describes other specialized ninja equipment, and the game master decides whether a ninja starts with any of it. The modern ninja favors technology in weapons and equipment. Money: 3D6x1000 credits, plus 4D4x1000 credits worth of black market salable items.

## Cybernetics

The character starts with cyber-armor and 1D4 implants of choice, plus a tracer chip the clan uses to keep track of him. Further implants must be purchased. See also the Ninja ''Borg.
